						"value": 24
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "TUNNEL\n\nIn this example we use shapes and feedback to create a lightweight tunnel source. There are a few things to learn here. Press the play button to start.\n\nWe use instances turn a single circle into a collection of 50 circles.\n\nWe use some clever math involving cos and sin to create some smooth animation.\n\nWe use feedback (patching the video mixer into itself) to create the illusion of infinity.\n\nWe purposefully did not use any interactive nodes like Color In or Float In. We like to give that challenge to you. See where you can add some interactive elements, save the patch as a source and test it in Resolume."
					}
				},
